From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] util.h: make VERSION and progname extern declarations

Upstream util.h defines two non-static global variables:

    const char *VERSION;
    const char *progname;

Every translation unit that #includes "util.h" emits a definition
of these symbols. GNU ld silently deduplicates them, but lld
(used by the OHOS toolchain) rejects the duplicates at link time:

    ld.lld: error: duplicate symbol: VERSION
    ld.lld: error: duplicate symbol: progname

Promote the header definitions to `extern` declarations and add a
single tentative definition of progname in util.c (VERSION already
has its definition there).
---
 src/util.c | 1 +
 src/util.h | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/util.c b/src/util.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/util.c
+++ b/src/util.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 
 #define INPUT_BUFFER_SIZE 102400
 
+const char *progname = "";
 const char *VERSION = "2.2.0";
 
 /* Print program version to stdout. */
diff --git a/src/util.h b/src/util.h
index 3333333..4444444 100644
--- a/src/util.h
+++ b/src/util.h
@@ -11,8 +11,8 @@
 #define MIN(a, b) ((a) < (b) ? (a) : (b))
 #define MAX(a, b) ((a) > (b) ? (a) : (b))
 
-const char *VERSION;
-const char *progname;
+extern const char *VERSION;
+extern const char *progname;
 
 // Subsampling method, which defines how much of the data from
 // each color channel is included in the image per 2x2 block.
-- 
2.39.1
